{"id": "67c8dbad", "ts": 1792295136.334751, "job": "11c1c622", "type": "review.verdict", "actor": "captain", "data": {"verdict": "FAIL", "review": "### Review:\n\n1. **Does it meet the spec?**\n   - The provided code snippet is a Cypress test script for an application, not the actual implementation of EvalCraft. Therefore, it does not meet the spec as it does not include the actual HTML, CSS, or JavaScript code for the application. The test script seems to be designed for a different application with features like login, profile editing, and mobile responsiveness, which are not part of the EvalCraft spec.\n\n2. **Bugs found:**\n   - Since the actual application code is missing, it is impossible to identify bugs based on the provided test script alone. However, the test script itself has some issues:\n     - It references routes (`/home`, `/login`, `/dashboard`, `/profile`) that are not mentioned in the EvalCraft spec.\n     - It assumes the existence of elements (`#login-button`, `#email`, `#password`, etc.) that are not specified in the EvalCraft requirements.\n     - The error handling in the test script is incomplete and does not provide meaningful assertions.\n\n3. **One-line verdict:**\n   - **FAIL**"}}
