{"id": "0e18572a", "ts": 1792295178.107989, "job": "11c1c622", "type": "review.verdict", "actor": "captain", "data": {"verdict": "FAIL", "review": "This code is a **skeleton/boilerplate** and fails to implement nearly all requirements of the specification.\n\n### 1. Does it meet the spec?\n**No.**\n*   **Missing Features:** It lacks the Rubric Builder (CRUD), Output Scorer (weighted math), Practice Mode (sample data/comparison), and History (localStorage).\n*   **Missing Design Requirements:** There is no dark mode toggle.\n*   **Technical Violation:** The spec requires a **single HTML file** with embedded CSS/JS. This submission is split into three separate files.\n*   **Functionality:** The \"Evaluation\" form is a placeholder that only echoes a single text string; it does not perform scoring or weighting.\n\n### 2. Bugs found\n*   **Persistence:** No data is saved to `localStorage`; all state is lost on refresh.\n*   **Navigation:** The \"Home\" section is visible by default, but clicking \"Home\" in the menu doesn't handle the initial state transition cleanly if other sections were added.\n*   **Logic:** The `toggleMenuButton` logic is brittle; if the CSS doesn't explicitly set `display: block`, the first click may do nothing because `style.display` starts as an empty string.\n*   **Missing UI:** There is no way to input AI text, assign weights, or view history as required.\n\n### 3. Verdict\n**FAIL**"}}
